{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5441892/academic-advisor": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01718 Division Academic Affairs Department Student Success Center Opening Date 08/10/2026 Control Number 8918 Description Benefits Job Summary Serve as an Academic Advisor to majors as assigned in the Student Success Center, which offers support services to ULM students. For students that have declared an academic major, the focus will be on early intervention and strengthening academic and/or college survival skills. Career planning will be offered as needed. Duties and Responsibilities Provides academic advising, including analysis and integration, for new and continuing college students, collegiate students, specifically, for all disciplines advised in the Clarke M. Williams Student Success Center. Provides academic advising assistance for majors other than those stated above to all colleges across campus. This assistance may be pre-advising sessions, training to faculty advisors, materials development and creation, as needed. Provides career planning, helping students make decisions on college majors and career opportunities. Collaborates with Career Connections and refers students to career information. Makes students aware of campus and community resources. Resolves problems related to curriculum, course prerequisites, and eligibility by referring to catalogues and other appropriate resource material. Evaluates transfer credits and applicability of academic credit to program requirements. Collaborates as a team member on development, coordination, and implementation of student retention initiatives, workshops, and other related programs. Remains up-to-date regarding university policies, procedures, and student requirements; includes familiarity with student handbooks, ULM catalogs, degree requirements, drop/adds, financial aid, etc. Collects data and participates in assessment of services. Creates reports and maintains student files. Uses technology to enhance delivery of service to students. Attends staff meetings and training sessions, and maintains currency in profession. Participates on college committees as needed. Assists in the development and implementation of Student Success Center materials. May supervise undergraduate and graduate student employees; may participate in training and evaluative sessions and recommend methods to improve performance. Plays an instrumental role in the processing, support services, and referrals related to the Beginning Freshmen Initiative and other retention programs. Prepares for and teaches the University Seminar (UNIV 1001 & 1010) each fall and spring semester; prepares and teaches other university classes in appropriate content areas as directed. Works with target students like scholarship recipients, emerging scholars, non-traditional students, and other groups as needed. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree related to the duties and responsibilities specified. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/3665780/adjunct-faculty": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Part-Time Job Number 00938 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Arts, Education, & Sciences Opening Date 08/03/2022 Control Number 0000 Description Benefits Job Summary The University of Louisiana Monroe’s School of Sciences is searching for adjunct faculty who have a passion for teaching: Some areas we may have needs for in the upcoming semesters are: Mathematics Chemistry Geography Geosciences Duties and Responsibilities Under the direction of the Director of the School, the adjunct’s responsibilities include: Teach assigned class material Follow the course syllabus with the course schedule Evaluate student performance through graded summative and formative assessments promptly and accurately Maintain records of student attendance, involvement, and progress Submit midterm and final grades Complete the required university and state training Minimum Qualifications The candidate should possess a Master’s Degree or PhD in Mathematics, Chemistry, Geography, and/or Geosciences, or a related field. Supplemental Information Required attachments: Cover Letter CV Employees are eligible to earn leave, and may be eligible for other benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5488983/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-computer-information-systems-program-coordin": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Computer Information Systems, Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Computer Information Systems, Program Coordinator Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01785 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Business & Social Scienc Opening Date 09/21/2026 Control Number 9027 Description Benefits Job Summary Candidates are expected to fulfill the role of Program Coordinator and must be able to contribute to the undergraduate Computer Information Systems program and should have broad competence in Information Systems with the ability to teach a variety of courses including business analytics, programming, management information systems, application development, project management, database development, telecommunications, and/or information security. The area of specialization is open, but the leading needs are in data analytics and application development. Opportunities also exist to teach graduate and summer classes. Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses during the fall and spring semesters Coordinate the activities of the program, including course scheduling, recruiting, industry outreach, academic support programs, and placement of students upon graduation. Pursue a program of scholarly research and publication Advise students and maintain records of student progress Actively participate in recruitment and retention for the program Engage with IT related industry groups and companies Perform other job-related duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have a doctoral degree in computer information systems or related field from an AACSB accredited institution. Rank will be determined based upon educational background, scholarly productivity, and academic experience. The ideal candidate will have: (1) Excellent teaching skills; (2) Evidence of the ability to perform quality applied, basic, or instructional research in the information systems field; (3) An established or planned research agenda; (4) Good interpersonal skills; (5) Effective written and oral communication skills, (6) The ability to work with and supervise a highly diverse student population, and (7) The ability to function collegially as a member of the faculty. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/4884122/assistant-professor-of-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01513 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Arts, Education, & Sciences Opening Date 03/26/2025 Control Number 8584 Description Benefits Job Summary The Biology Program within the School of Sciences at the University of Louisiana at Monroe (ULM) is seeking an Assistant Professor of Biology for Fall 2025 or Spring 2026. The School of Sciences offers a bachelor’s degree in Biology with concentrations in Premedical Studies, Wildlife and Natural Resource Conservation, Evolution & Ecology, and Molecular Biology & Biotechnology. The School of Sciences also offers a master’s degree in Biology. Duties and Responsibilities • Teach undergraduate and graduate courses during the fall and spring semesters. • Mentor graduate students and graduate student research projects. • Pursue a program of scholarly research and publication. • Advise students and maintain records of student progress. • Actively participate in recruitment and retention for the Biology degree program. • Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must be passionate about teaching and mentoring students. Candidates should have a doctoral degree in biology. ABD candidates in late stages of dissertation will also be considered. Qualifications include: • Innovative pedagogical approaches to teaching undergraduates from diverse backgrounds • Coursework and/or experience in Biology • Ability to teach a diverse set of undergraduate or graduate level molecular biology classes including genetics • Effective oral and written communication skills • A research agenda or demonstration of scholarly activity Supplemental Information N/A Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5325877/assistant-professor-of-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01661 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Arts, Education, & Sciences Opening Date 04/29/2026 Control Number 8857 Description Benefits Job Summary The Department of Biology at the University of Louisiana Monroe invites applications for a faculty position in Biology. We seek an energetic, student-centered educator with a Ph.D. in a relevant biological science discipline who is passionate about teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. The department seeks a faculty member to teach classes for a growing instructional need in organismal biology. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching foundational and upper-level courses that explore the relationships between biological form and physiological processes. Research experiences for both plant and animal model organisms will be considered, with preference for plant biology. Duties and Responsibilities • Teach undergraduate and graduate courses during the fall and spring semester. • Advise students and maintain records of student progress. • Actively participate in recruitment and retention for the Biology degree program. • Assist in all areas of program improvement, including participation in curriculum development, evaluation, and assessment. • Pursue a program of scholarly research and publication. • Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must be passionate about teaching undergraduates. Candidates should have a earned a PhD in Biology or related disciplined. Qualifications include: • Innovative pedagogical approaches to teaching undergraduates from diverse backgrounds • Coursework and/or experience in biology or related field • A research agenda or demonstration of scholarly activity • Effective oral and written communication skills. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5491701/assistant-associate-professor-of-psychology": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01786 Division Academic Affairs Department School of Behavioral & Social Sci Opening Date 09/22/2026 Control Number 9033 Description Benefits Job Summary The University of Louisiana Monroe invites applications for an Assistant/Associate Professor of Psychology and Graduate Program Coordinator. This is a face-to-face position that involves regular, daily interaction with students, faculty, and university staff. The role balances reduced teaching responsibilities with substantial administrative coordination for our graduate psychology programs Duties and Responsibilities To accommodate administrative duties, the teaching load is set at two to three courses per semester. Responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across a variety of topics, including advanced statistics and forensic psychology. Experienced both online and face-to-face teaching, including large classes Maintaining an active presence on campus to support student learning, advising, and professional mentorship. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or Psy. D. in Psychology from an American University (state licensure in psychology preferred). Familiarity with advanced statistics and quantitative methods History of peer-reviewed research and publications Preference given to candidates with a background or specialization in forensic psychology Supplemental Information Program Management & Year-Round Expectations: The coordinator manages an online and face-to-face graduate program of approximately 150 students with rolling admissions throughout the year. Because admissions and student processing occur continuously, this position requires active involvement during academic breaks and summer sessions. Additional duties include overseeing all graduate admissions, student coordination, academic advising, directing master’s theses, and recruitment and career preparation activities. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5206656/assistant-associate-professor-physical-therapy": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor Physical Therapy Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 12-month Faculty Job Number 01601 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Health Sciences Opening Date 01/21/2026 Control Number 8762 & 8761 Description Benefits Job Summary The University of Louisiana Monroe invites applications for a full-time 12-month tenure-track faculty position in the developing DPT program. The Assistant or Associate Professor holds a faculty appointment and has administrative, academic, service, and scholarship responsibilities consistent with the mission and philosophy of the academic program. Duties and Responsibilities Duties and Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Developing, monitoring, and refining the neuromuscular, geriatric, pediatric, professional development, sex, gender, or gender expression based, or practice management components of the curriculum Facilitating quality learning experiences for students Evaluating students' performance, in cooperation with other faculty, to determine their ability to integrate didactic and clinical learning experiences and to progress within the curriculum Conducting research in their area of expertise Providing service to the DPT Program, Department, College, University and/or the Profession Minimum Qualifications Graduate of an accredited physical therapist professional program or deemed equivalent non-accredited program Earned clinical doctoral degree in physical therapy or an earned academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc) Licensed or eligible for licensure in the state where employed Minimum of 3 years of experience as a licensed physical therapist Minimum of at least one year of clinical teaching or clinical coordination experience Strong communication, organization, interpersonal, problem-solving, and counseling skills Current knowledge and skill in the use of information and computer technology (e.g., word processing, e-mail, database) or proven ability to learn these skills Able to work with students with special needs based on the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) Design and conduct independent and/or collaborative research in clinical education or related areas Preferred Qualification or Requirements Neuromuscular, Pediatric, Geriatric, or Sex, Gender, or Gender Expression Content Expertise Holds a nationally recognized certification for advanced clinical practice through the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties or other institution Practice management experience Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5410774/athletic-academic-counselor": {
      "title": "Athletic Academic Counselor",
      "description": "Athletic Academic Counselor Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01732 Division Athletics Opening Date 07/15/2026 Control Number 8953 & 8919 Description Benefits Job Summary This position serves as an academic counselor offering academic support services to student-athletes. Duties and Responsibilities This position reports directly to the Associate Director of Athletic Academics, and the Director of Athletic Academics. The duties and responsibilities for this position include: Maintaining the highest standard of integrity through compliance with all University, Sun Belt Conference and NCAA rules and regulations Responsible for identifying and addressing the academic needs of student-athletes in the sports assigned, by providing, or arranging for the provision of, academic support services Maintaining accurate and complete records on assigned student-athletes Monitoring the academic progress of student-athletes throughout the academic year, to include: Providing academic counseling assistance in the areas of course selection and registration for student-athletes assigned to this position Monitoring and approving classes to be added/dropped by assigned student-athletes, including counseling students about such matters Reviewing and approving curriculum/major changes processed by assigned student athletes, including counseling students about such matters Assisting student-athletes to understand the nature and purpose of a University education and guide student-athletes toward individual responsibility, to include directing the student-athlete to: Become familiar with University policies, registration procedures and regulations Utilize all of the University's resources Obtain information about numerous academic programs available Assume responsibility for planning and monitoring his or her academic progress Develop a sense of belonging within the University Communicating regularly with the Interim Director of the Student Success Center, Coordinator of Academic Counseling, the Assistant Director of Athletics for Academic and Compliance, and the Head Coach (or designee) regarding academic programming and the academic and eligibility status of assigned student-athletes Communicating with advisors and faculty as needed in order to provide appropriate support to student-athletes Reviewing academic credentials of prospective student-athletes and providing recommendations to the coaching staff Meeting with prospective student-athletes, parents and others during regular office hours and occasional weekends during heavy recruiting periods Coordinate the NCAA Academic Performance Program Other duties include: Keeping up-to-date information on Department, University, Sun Belt Conference and NCAA policies and bylaws Serving as referral agent to other University services Attending staff meetings and participating in appropriate professional development and office activities Assisting in coordination of Supervised Study and Mentoring Programs Performing other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field is required, Master’s degree in a related field is preferred. Professional experience in intercollegiate athletics is desirable, direct experience with academic counseling is ideal. Excellent communication skills, both written and oral, and the ability to work occasional nights and weekends is required. Supplemental Information Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5487528/cohs-recruitment-and-retention-coach": {
      "title": "COHS - Recruitment and Retention Coach",
      "description": "COHS - Recruitment and Retention Coach Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01784 Division Academic Affairs Department Kitty DeGree School of Nursing Opening Date 09/18/2026 Control Number 9030 Description Benefits Job Summary Serves as the recruitment and retention coach for the School of Nursing and Radiologic Technology. Also serves on the KDSON Recruitment and Retention Committee. Primary responsibility is to oversee promotional and marketing of programs and recruiting and retention efforts for Kitty DeGree School of Nursing and Radiologic Technology. Provide administrative support to the Program Directors in the School of Nursing and Radiologic Technology program. Duties and Responsibilities Track, analyze, and organize data related to student recruitment, engagement, progression, persistence, and retention within the Nursing and Radiologic Technology programs to identify trends, barriers, and opportunities for improvement. Develop and implement proactive student retention initiatives in collaboration with Nursing and Radiologic Technology faculty, program leadership, advising, and student support services. Monitor student progression and identify students who may be at risk for attrition based on academic performance, course progression, attendance, engagement, or other established indicators; assist with appropriate outreach and referral to campus resources. Maintain regular communication with current students to promote engagement, connection to the program, and awareness of academic, professional, and student support resources. Assist in developing and coordinating student engagement activities designed to strengthen students’ sense of belonging, connection to their programs, and commitment to degree completion. Assist Nursing and Radiologic Technology programs in developing and implementing strategies to improve semester-to-semester persistence, progression, and program completion. Collect and maintain retention-related data and prepare reports for program leadership to support data-informed retention planning and continuous improvement. Track student participation in retention initiatives and evaluate the effectiveness of interventions and activities designed to improve student persistence and completion. Create cohesive recruitment and retention marketing efforts in collaboration with Nursing and Radiologic Technology. Collaborate with recruiting, advising, student success, retention entities, and other campus partners to coordinate recruitment, student engagement, and retention outreach across campus. Work with the Office of Marketing and Communications to ensure recruitment and retention efforts follow official university marketing standards and messaging. Participate in university-wide recruitment, student engagement, and outreach events. Assist with outreach to prospective and current students through appropriate communication channels to provide timely information, encourage engagement, and facilitate connection to university and program resources. Assist with maintaining organized and secure records related to prospective and current students in accordance with university policies and applicable privacy requirements. Assists in maintaining and tracking departmental inventory related to recruitment, student engagement, and retention activities. Assists in ordering supplies, equipment, promotional materials, and other resources related to recruitment, student engagement, and retention activities. Exhibits appropriate and consistent written and oral communication skills when interacting with faculty, students, staff, prospective students, university partners, and/or clients within the assigned area. Creates and maintains prospective student and current student files and records in accordance with established university policies and procedures. Assists with the development of reports, tracking systems, dashboards, and other tools used to monitor recruitment, enrollment, student progression, persistence, and retention outcomes. Attend and complete yearly and/or quarterly training for safety, ethics, Title IX, FERPA, and other mandatory university training requirements. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred. Strong organization, analytical, attention to detail, and communication (spoken and written) skills and computer skills (Microsoft Word, Excel, Power Point) mandatory. Available to work 40 hours per week. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends for program-sponsored events. Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse population. Ability to maintain confidentiality of records and all office discussions and procedures Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, faculty, and staff Able to multitask. Must have a strong ability to work cross functionally with other essential offices. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5491691/director-of-admissions-operations": {
      "title": "Director of Admissions Operations",
      "description": "Director of Admissions Operations Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01782 Division Academic Affairs Department Admissions Opening Date 09/22/2026 Control Number 9020 Description Benefits Job Summary The Director of Admissions Operations provides leadership and oversight for the operational functions of the Office of Admissions Operations. This position is responsible for managing admissions processing activities, supervising office personnel, ensuring the integrity and accuracy of applicant and student data, and coordinating administrative processes that support enrollment goals and university policies. The Director works collaboratively with academic and administrative departments across the institution to facilitate efficient admissions services, maintain compliance with applicable regulations, prepare required reports, and provide a high level of customer service to prospective students, families, faculty, staff, and external constituents. Duties and Responsibilities Direct and oversee the daily operations of the Office of Admissions Operations. Supervise, train, evaluate, and develop admissions operations staff and student employees. Ensure timely and accurate processing of applications, transcripts, residency documents, test scores, and other admission-related materials. Oversee verification, maintenance, and quality control of applicant and student records to ensure data accuracy and integrity. Monitor and manage admissions workflows to ensure compliance with university policies, state and federal regulations, and established service standards. Utilize student information systems, admissions technologies, and reporting tools to support admissions operations and enrollment objectives. Prepare, analyze, and distribute admissions-related reports for university leadership, state agencies, accreditation organizations, and other internal/external stakeholders. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Registrar, Institutional Research, Information Technology, Financial Aid, Student Affairs, and other campus departments to support enrollment management initiatives and student success efforts. Serve as a resource for admissions policies, procedures, and operational requirements. Manages scholarship awarding for undergraduates. Respond to and resolve complex admissions and records issues requiring interpretation of policies and regulations. Develop, document, and implement operational procedures to improve efficiency, effectiveness, and customer service. Assist with system implementations, upgrades, testing, and process improvement initiatives related to admissions operations. Support strategic enrollment initiatives through data analysis, reporting, and operational planning. Ensure a welcoming, student-centered environment that promotes exceptional customer service. Serve on university committees and work groups as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Demonstrated evidence of progressively responsible experience in admissions, enrollment management, student services, records management, higher education administration, or a related field. Experience supervising and leading professional and/or support staff. Experience working with database systems and administrative software applications. Strong analytical, organizational, policy interpretation, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and external constituents. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5504698/grants-manager": {
      "title": "Grants Manager",
      "description": "Grants Manager Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01790 Division Business Affairs Department Controller Opening Date 10/05/2026 Control Number 9042 Description Benefits Job Summary This professional staff position reports directly to the Controller in all accounting matters and works very closely with the Office of Sponsored Programs and Research. The primary functions of this position are post-award activities related to financial accounting and reporting for various local, state, and federal grants and contracts. Responsibilities include assisting grant developers/researchers in budget development, monitoring and approval of expenditures, preparation of financial reports to include reimbursement requests, draw down of federal cash and submission of various financial reports as required by the funding agencies. Duties and Responsibilities Collaborates with Sponsored Programs Administration and other University departments to support the effective administration of grants, contracts, and sponsored programs. Reviews post-award documentation to ensure compliance with sponsor requirements, University policies, applicable regulations, and award terms and conditions. Establishes and maintains grant accounts, financial records, award files, and related documentation to support accurate financial management and reporting throughout the grant lifecycle. Processes grant-related financial transactions, including journal entries, budget adjustments, cost transfers, matching fund transfers, and other accounting activities in accordance with established policies and procedures. Reviews grant expenditures to ensure allowability, proper documentation, and compliance with approved budgets, sponsor requirements, and institutional guidelines. Monitors grant financial activity, including expenditures, available balances, receivables, cash activity, reporting requirements, and project closeout deadlines, identifying and assisting in the resolution of discrepancies as needed. Prepares and submits grant invoices, reimbursement requests, drawdown requests, and other sponsor-required documentation in a timely and accurate manner. Establishes new accounts in BANNER and close accounts after termination dates in accordance with established procedures; ensure all required reports are sent to sponsor for project termination. Maintains billing and reporting schedules, records and reconciles grant receivables, and follows up on outstanding balances to support effective cash management and compliance with sponsor requirements. Establishes grant accounts and coordinates award closeout activities, including final reconciliations, account termination, and submission of required sponsor reports and documentation. Provides guidance and assistance to faculty, staff, and researchers regarding grant administration procedures, financial requirements, account status, reporting obligations, and compliance matters. Supervises, monitors and coordinates work activities of direct report. Assists with other duties in the Controller’s Office as deemed necessary. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Accounting or related field is required. Must be able to communicate effectively with regulatory authorities and university professional level staff. Prior supervisory experience and experience with governmental and/or fund accounting preferred. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5502461/instructor-of-accounting": {
      "title": "Instructor of Accounting",
      "description": "Instructor of Accounting Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01788 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Business & Social Scienc Opening Date 10/01/2026 Control Number 9025 Description Benefits Job Summary The College is seeking an instructor of Accounting. Candidates are expected to contribute primarily to the BBA in Accounting program. The Accounting Program is accredited by AACSB-International . The candidate should have broad competence in Accounting with the ability to teach a variety of face-to-face and online courses. Candidates who bring experience, expertise, and/or specialization in Financial Accounting are most preferred. Effective teaching skill must be demonstrated and is expected in both online and face-to-face classes. Duties and Responsibilities Teach primarily undergraduate courses during the fall and spring semesters. Mentor undergraduate students. Pursue a program of effective teaching, mentoring, and community engagement. Advise students and maintain records of student progress. Actively participate in recruitment and retention for the programs. Contribute to the mission of the program and college. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Candidates are preferred to have, at a minimum, a master’s degree in Accounting or closely related field of specialization, and must demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and service. Expertise should be demonstrated through academic transcripts and/or professional experience. Candidates' experience should reflect a strong background in financial accounting, with governmental accounting knowledge considered a strong plus. ULM is seeking applications from candidates who can also demonstrate aptitude in teaching and working with individuals with diverse backgrounds and contribute to the University’s mission, vision, and core values. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5502481/instructor-assistant-or-associate-professor-of-disaster-management-program-coord": {
      "title": "Instructor, Assistant or Associate Professor of Disaster Management-Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Instructor, Assistant or Associate Professor of Disaster Management-Program Coordinator Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01789 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Business & Social Scienc Opening Date 10/01/2026 Control Number 8940 Description Benefits Job Summary The University of Louisiana Monroe (ULM) invites applications for a full-time, nine-month faculty appointment at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, or Associate Professor in Disaster Management. The successful candidate will also serve as Program Coordinator for ULM’s new Bachelor of Science in Disaster Management, launched in Fall 2026 within the School of Construction Management. Rank and appointment type will be commensurate with the candidate’s education, experience, scholarly record, and ULM criteria. The program prepares students to help communities and organizations anticipate risk, sustain readiness, respond effectively, and recover from natural, technological, and human-caused disasters. ULM seeks a collaborative teacher-scholar or scholar-practitioner with broad competence in disaster and emergency management who can teach across the curriculum in both face-to-face and online formats and help build a distinctive, practice-connected program. Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in disaster management, emergency management, and related areas during the fall and spring semesters in face-to-face and online formats. Coordinate the Disaster Management program in collaboration with the School Director, including course scheduling, curriculum sequencing, adjunct coordination, and routine program operations. Lead curriculum mapping, student-learning assessment, continuous improvement, program review, and documentation needed for institutional and specialized-accreditation readiness, including monitoring emerging ACCE criteria relevant to Disaster Management. Advise and mentor undergraduate students; maintain accurate records of student progress; and support timely progression and graduation. Participate actively in student recruitment, enrollment growth, retention initiatives, internships, career development, and alumni engagement. Build and sustain relationships with local, parish, state, federal, nonprofit, healthcare, private-sector, and professional emergency-management partners; support an active external advisory group. For tenure-track appointments, pursue a sustained program of scholarly research, publication, and externally engaged work appropriate to rank and faculty qualification expectations. Contribute to the missions of the program, School, College, and University through service, professional engagement, and regular participation in on-campus activities and events. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Broad academic or professional competence in disaster management, emergency management, homeland security, public safety, public administration, disaster science, resilience, hazard mitigation, or a closely related field. Evidence of effective college-level teaching—or strong potential for effective teaching—across both online and face-to-face formats. Ability to teach and mentor students from varied educational, professional, and personal backgrounds and to contribute to ULM’s mission, vision, and core values. Ability to meet ULM and College faculty qualification requirements appropriate to the rank, appointment type, and assigned courses. Rank-specific qualifications Instructor. A master’s degree in disaster management, emergency management, homeland security, public safety, public administration, disaster science, resilience, or a closely related field from an accredited institution, plus substantial relevant professional experience. If the graduate degree is outside the assigned teaching discipline, the candidate must document at least 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching field or an approved equivalent basis for qualification. Assistant Professor. An earned doctorate or other appropriate terminal degree in a field listed above by the appointment date. ABD candidates may be considered only if degree completion by the appointment date is documented. Candidates must show clear potential for excellence in teaching, research, and service. Associate Professor. An earned doctorate or other appropriate terminal degree in a field listed above and a record of effective teaching, peer-reviewed scholarship, professional engagement, and service commensurate with ULM requirements for appointment at the associate rank. Preferred qualifications Certified Emergency Manager (CEM®) credential from the International Association of Emergency Managers; Louisiana Emergency Manager (LEM), Master Exercise Practitioner (MEP), or another relevant professional credential is also valued. Five or more years of progressively responsible experience in comprehensive emergency management, disaster operations, mitigation, recovery, resilience, business continuity, public safety, or a closely related area. Experience coordinating or launching an academic program, developing curriculum, mapping learning outcomes, conducting assessment, preparing accreditation or program-review materials, or leading continuous improvement. Expertise in one or more high-need areas such as hazard mitigation and risk assessment, disaster recovery, GIS and geospatial analysis, climate and community resilience, emergency planning and exercises, crisis communication, public health preparedness, critical infrastructure, or business continuity. A record of online course design and delivery, applied or community-engaged scholarship, externally funded work, or partnerships with emergency-management agencies and professional associations. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5254160/instructor-assistant-associate-professor-nursing": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor Nursing",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor Nursing Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01625 Division Academic Affairs Department Kitty DeGree School of Nursing Opening Date 03/02/2026 Control Number 8771 Description Benefits Job Summary The Nursing Faculty is actively engaged in course delivery and is responsible for the assessment, planning, implementation, grading, course creation, proctoring, test review, and evaluation of assigned courses. The Nursing Faculty evaluates the performance of students and mentors students with a focus on student retention and RN licensure. Duties and Responsibilities Mentor students scoring at or below 78 in coursework and actively take student appointments for individual and group mentoring sessions Participate in all responsibilities of teaching courses, including student orientation, grading assignments, discussion posts, exams, and any other course assessments Participate in all aspects of test review for assigned courses Participate in all course responsibilities and assignments related to teaching, grading, assessing courses, retaining students, and contributing actively as a course instructor, whether teaching in a team or as an individual Grade assignments, proctor exams, review tests, and engage in course delivery Teach a full-time teaching load, which includes a core nursing course and a clinical each semester Participate in all aspects of facilitating test proctoring, test item writing, proctoring, and test review Create lectures, content, and materials for courses Work on retention and persistence of students, including calling, emailing, and reaching out to students with a focus on student retention and completion Participate in test reviews, standardized testing reviews, to prepare students appropriately for course success and NCLEX testing Attend pinning ceremonies and other events and activities as assigned Submit time sheet and request for time off on time Submit midterm and final grades on time Act as mentor and role model for students in classroom and clinical, including Skills Lab and Simulation Lab. First-semester \"clinical\" includes skills lab, simulation lab, and hospital clinical time for anyone teaching clinical whether full-time or part-time. Facilitate learning of relevant course material Evaluate students’ academic and clinical performance Maintain office schedule for advisement and consultation Serve as faculty advisor to student organizations when such service is required Develop/maintain syllabi and course content in the Learning Management System Maintain accurate scholastic records and abide by FERPA policies Show evidence of professional development through activities such as continuing education, certifications, professional organizations, volunteering at a free clinic, etc. If outside employment in an educational or clinical setting is desired, it must not conflict with duties to Kitty DeGree School of Nursing. Participate in Nursing Faculty meetings Participate in activities to maintain Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) accreditation and Louisiana State Board of Nursing approval Ensure continued program quality and productivity through participation in faculty inservices and annual advisory committee meetings with clinical agency personnel and alumni Participate in recruitment, admission, and enrollment activities Foster open communication with all departments within the institution to facilitate negotiations and good working relationships Contribute to the overall college mission through participation in college committees Teach course in accordance with the class schedule and course syllabi Participate in faculty committees as assigned Conduct self in the best interest of the KDSON and ULM at all times Maintain collaborative relationships with professional and health care agencies Represent the nursing department in relevant community functions Participate in activities to promote the profession of nursing Familiarize self with KDSON, COHS, and ULM policies and procedures The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment to the position. Minimum Qualifications A master’s or higher degree in nursing or A baccalaureate degree in nursing plus evidence of continued progress toward a master’s or higher degree in nursing Evidence of current practice with a minimum of two (2) years full-time equivalent practice as a Registered nurse in a clinical setting preceding the first date of first employment as a teacher. Communication and leadership skills Scope and practice of Baccalaureate Nurses Expertise in course material and continuing education in the subjects taught Some familiarity with guidelines for accreditation by Louisiana State Board of Nursing (LSBN) and the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) Supplemental Information Special Requirements: Hold a valid unencumbered license to practice as a Registered Nurse in Louisiana All nursing faculty shall participate in research projects, surveys, professional writing, continuing education, academic study, or clinical practice to improve own nursing competence in areas of responsibility Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5382263/network-telecommunications-specialist-2": {
      "title": "Network & Telecommunications Specialist 2",
      "description": "Network & Telecommunications Specialist 2 Salary $48,000.00 - $58,000.00 Annually Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01704 Division Information Services and Student Success Opening Date 06/18/2026 Control Number 8900 Description Benefits Job Summary Closely supervised, mid-level position. Successful candidate will participate in the immediate support of Campus Networking infrastructures and Telecom. Assist with network support and troubleshooting of main Campus Academic/Administrative networks as well as Residential Life networks for student residents. Will assist Telecom Coordinator as needed in the daily management of Phone system and related resources through-out Campus. Duties and Responsibilities Utilize centralized Helpdesk tracking software for all levels of customer service engagement. Triage Helpdesk calls for all network requests from across campus including phone issues. Assist network administrator in the planning, expansion, and troubleshooting of ULM campus networks. Assist telecomm coordinator in the daily support of phone system environment. Works in a support/resolution role for technical issues when Students experience Internet access problems within Residential Life facilities. Includes WiFi and LAN-lines in residence rooms. Coordinate with Residential Life when interaction is required with residents for network troubleshooting. Work with other IT staff when needed for support resolution. Required to work afterhours in the event of unexpected or planned outages. Assist IT security officer in operational network support of surveillance cameras and door security controllers. Engage with 3 rd party cabling contractors for new cabling requests or repairs. Other duties as required. Minimum Qualifications Required to have a bachelor degree with a concentration in computer networks, one or more network certifications, and 1 year of internship in enterprise network systems. OR 5+ years of real-world field experience with enterprise grade networks and network systems. Working ethernet Layer 1-3 knowledge is required. Certification or knowledge of Juniper/JUNOS/Mist is preferred. Optical networking knowledge is useful. Experience in all desktop/server types (Windows/Linux) Certification or proven field knowledge in cabled networks including fiber optic standards, CAT5/6 and POE standards. Knowledge in phone systems infrastructure is useful. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5459764/sonography-program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Sonography Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Sonography Program Coordinator Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 12-month Faculty Job Number 01766 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Health Sciences Opening Date 08/25/2026 Control Number 9001 Description Benefits Job Summary Responsible for all aspects of the program, including the administration, planning, continuous review, development, and general effectiveness of the program as well as all duties as defined for full-time faculty. Responsibilities also include meeting and maintaining program accreditation requirements, systematic review of program effectiveness among didactic, laboratory, and clinical components, student recruitment, committee assignments and serving as a liaison with health care facilities. Duties and Responsibilities 1. Administers, directs, and organizes the entire program. 2.Formulates the curriculum and writes course outlines for all professional courses. 3.Previews and critiques instructor lesson plans, visual aids, student instructional handouts, and summary materials. 4.Arranges with clinical affiliates for practical experience phases of training. 5.Directs classes and demonstration sessions in technical aspects of Diagnostic Medical Sonography. 6.Coordinates the pre-professional curriculum with other university departments. 7.Assigns adjunct faculty to various teaching responsibilities, as required. 8.Evaluates the entire curriculum and makes periodic revisions. 9.Selects course textbooks and recommends the purchase of library textbooks. 10.Participates in student recruitment and student selection for the professional program. 11.Evaluates the academic and clinical progress of the student. 12.Acts as a liaison between the Diagnostic Medical Sonography program and University officials. 13.Conducts regular faculty meetings and affiliation visits. 14.Counsels and advises students in the program. 15.Assists in developing the program budget with the appropriate university officials. 16.Prepares purchase orders for all supplies and equipment for the program. 17.Has responsibility for maintenance of academic class records and records of former students, including current positions and/or locations. 18.Handles all correspondence for the Diagnostic Medical Sonography program. 19.Represents the program at state and local meetings. 20.Formulates policies and procedures for the professional program. 21.Serves on University and College committees as needed. 22.Makes job recommendations and assists in the placement of graduates. 23.Writes grant applications and progress reports. 24.Develops and participates in continuing education programs. Minimum Qualifications Baccalaureate degree from an accredited college or university is required and current certification through the American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography (ARDMS). 2.Minimum of four (4) years of experience as a registered diagnostic medical sonographer, of which two (2) years must include experience in clinical diagnostic care and a minimum of two (2) years teaching in an accredited sonography program either as an appointed faculty member or as a clinical preceptor. 3.Qualifications shall assure proficiency in instructing, curriculum design, program planning and counseling. 4.Certified in good standing with American Registry for Diagnostic Medical Sonography (ARDMS) and hold a valid registered diagnostic medical sonography credential in abdominal and/or OB-GYN. Preferred Qualifications 1. Master’s degree or Doctorate degree in education or leadership from a regionally accredited college or university. 2. Five years of teaching and administrative experience in a college or university setting. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5517415/admissions-counselor": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01792 Division Academic Affairs Department Recruitment Opening Date 10/15/2026 Control Number 9044 Description Benefits Job Summary Recruit high school students, or transfer students to attend ULM. Duties and Responsibilities Build relationships with stakeholders at assigned schools Recruit assigned zone by attending college and career fairs, classroom visits, and lunch visits Complete recruitment package drop-offs at area schools Identify target schools in assigned zone(s) Schedule visits with each of the schools throughout the Fall and Spring semesters Correspond with students and parents throughout the recruitment and admissions process Correspond with High School Counselors year-round Work recru i ting events Lead campus tours as needed Substitute for other recruiters when travel overlaps Coordinate with faculty and staff in the recruitment of students at university events Follow up with students who have shown interest in the university Run enrollment reports through Recruit/ARGOS Be able to work extensively in Banner and any other university technology systems. Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Must possess a minimum of a bachelor's degree with appropriate experience in college admissions, student services, marketing, or related area. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
