    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5517071/clinical-assistant-professor-assistant-professor-of-pharmacy": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of Pharmacy",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor/Assistant Professor of Pharmacy Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 12-month Faculty Job Number 01794 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Pharmacy Opening Date 10/14/2026 Control Number 8941 Description Benefits Job Summary The position of Non-tenure track Assistant or Associate Professor in Pharmacy Practice has a multitude of responsibilities that center primarily around teaching and service. While all faculty are expected to be scholars, scholarship requirements for non-tenure track faculty are generally less than those for tenure-track faculty The position of Tenure-track Assistant/Associate or Full Professor in Pharmacy Practice has a multitude of responsibilities that are divided in the areas of teaching, service and scholarship. Tenure-track faculty are expected to develop a substantial program of scholarship that can withstand review from faculty at peer institutions. The Department describes scholarship in a broad sense, and expects that tenure track faculty will spend a significant amount of time pursuing and participating in scholarly activities Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Non-Tenure (40-60%) Tenure (30-50%) Teaching is a primary responsibility for tenure track Pharmacy Practice faculty. Faculty are expected to provide 20-40 didactic lectures as well as teach six to eight months/year in the Advanced Practice Experience Program. Didactic lectures may be taught on campus or through distance learning technology. Teaching responsibilities are at the discretion of the Department Head. Specific responsibilities may include. Coordination or Co-coordination of (a) team taught course(s). Provision of lectures in team taught courses. This responsibility includes providing appropriate exam questions covering the material taught in a timely manner. When appropriate, provision of a single instructor course (Serving as coordinator and lecturer) Precepting students in the Advanced Practice Experience Program. Precepting responsibilities include not only direct supervision of students in patient care encounters, but also appropriately conveying expectations at the beginning of the experience, individualized teaching, and providing formative feedback at the midpoint of the experience and summative feedback at the end of the experience formative feedback at the midpoint of the experience and summative feedback at the end of the experience Service: Non-Tenure (40-60%) Tenure (20-40% ) Service is the second area of primary responsibility for non-tenure track Pharmacy Practice faculty. The provision of professional services through contractual agreements with affiliated institutions is an important component of the position. Specific responsibilities may be delineated in a service contract; however, in general, responsibilities include: Provision of pharmaceutical care for a defined population of patients Documentation of the service, including the financial impact of the service on the affiliated institution and/or the patient population. When appropriate, seeking patient or third - party reimbursement for services. Serving as a member, secretary or other officer on committees at the affiliated institution with the approval of the Department Head. Serving as a member, secretary or chair of a Departmental, School, College or University committee. Participation in graduation ceremonies when assigned. Participation in Local, State and National Professional Organizations. Provision of Community service. Scholarship: Non-Tenure (5-10%) Tenure(20-50%) The Department expects that individual faculty will pursue the discovery, integration, and application of knowledge as well as try innovative teaching techniques in the classroom. The Department, College and University do expect that Clinical Sciences faculty will participate in the scholarship process when opportunity and time permit in the following ways: Poster presentations at State, National or International meetings Podium Presentations at State, National or International meetings Case-report or case-seriespublications Review articlepublication Peer-reviewed research articlepublication Serving as a manuscript or book reviewer for peer reviewedpublications When individual faculty have the interest and/or skill the pursuit of grant funding other scholarly activities is encouraged. Tenure The Department relies upon tenure-track faculty to support the Department with extramural funding and create national and international recognition for scholarship at the institution. Department does expect that individual faculty will pursue the discovery, integration, and application of knowledge as well as try innovative teaching techniques in the classroom. It is also expected that tenure-track faculty will aggressively pursue extramural funding for scholarly activities as well as publish in peer reviewed journals. Examples of desired Scholarly activities include Invited research symposia at State, Regional, National or International meetings Poster presentations at State, Regional, National or Internationalmeetings Podium Presentations at State, Regional, National or International meetings Peer-reviewed publication of Book Reviews Letters to the editor . Case-report or case-series publications . Review or systematic review articles Original research articles Book Chapters Books Serving as a manuscript or book reviewer for peer reviewed publication Pursuing and/or obtaining extramural funding for scholarlyactivities. Development of computer related programming for educational or research purposes. These items should be peer reviewable. Peer reviewable documentation demonstrating the quality and usefulness of novel Pharmaceutical Care Services or the application of new or novel models to your patient population. Minimum Qualifications Candidates should have a Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE accredited college/school of pharmacy (or equivalent) with residency and/or fellowship training. Those with equivalent experience in the area of practice will also be considered. Eligibility for Louisiana state pharmacy licensure is required. Board certification in a pharmacy care specialty is strongly desired. Candidates should exhibit effective verbal and written communication and interpersonal skills, and dedication to student-centered education and lifelong learning. Supplemental Information Promotion Non-Tenure: Promotion from Assistant to Associate and /or Associate to Professor will occur according to the guidelines set-fo1ih in the Department and University's guidelines; however, for non-tenure track faculty, the greatest emphasis will be placed in the areas of teaching and service Tenure: The awarding of tenure and the promotion from Assistant to Associate and /or Associate to Professor will occur according to the guidelines set-forth in the Department and University's guidelines; however, for tenure track faculty, the greatest emphasis will be placed in the areas of teaching and scholarly activities. Required Attachments: Please submit CV and Letter of Intent along with application Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5517103/pharmacist-quality-unit-support": {
      "title": "Pharmacist, Quality Unit Support",
      "description": "Pharmacist, Quality Unit Support Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01795 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Pharmacy Opening Date 10/14/2026 Control Number 9047 Description Benefits Job Summary This position may be located at the Louisiana Department of Health (LDH), in Baton Rouge, Louisiana, OR at the University Louisiana Monroe College of Pharmacy in Monroe, Louisiana, and involves support for the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program in the following areas: Medicaid Pharmacy Lock-In Program, 340B Drug Pricing Program, drug utilization review (DUR), pharmacy prior authorization, and other duties, such as audit and rebate, as directed by the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program. Duties and Responsibilities Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program, the fiscal intermediary, and University of Louisiana at Monroe (ULM) with the operations of the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program; Support the Medicaid Lock-In Program by evaluating selection criteria, reviewing profiles, managing recipients, communicating with providers, conducting research, and reporting; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program with the 340B Drug Pricing Program, including, but not limited to, the HRSA Medicaid Exclusion File and responding to questions/concerns from 340B Louisiana Medicaid providers; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program by responding to Pharmacy Help Desk calls from Medicaid stakeholders (recipients, providers, health plans, etc.); Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program by maintaining a local pharmacy list; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program in the management of physician-administered drugs, to include the review of MCO medical drug criteria and policies; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Rebate Program with drug related questions and reporting; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy program by reviewing and suggesting revisions to Medicaid Member Notifications; Draft provider notices regarding implementation of pharmacy-related Medicaid policy and procedure updates; Review and make recommendations for updates to the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Benefits Management Services Manual; Assist the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program in cross-over claim reconciliation; At the direction of the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program, extract and analyze pharmacy-related claims data from the P-Web database; Serve as report business owners for MCO quarterly and monthly reports; Support the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program with legislative fiscal impact questions and reporting; Research clinical questions and policy issues; Prepare management and utilization reports as directed by the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program; Work with other contractors on special applications/projects as directed by the Louisiana Medicaid Pharmacy Program (such as the POS User Guide, ECHO’s, etc.); Review of MCO Remittance Advices; Participate in disaster relief activities at the request of the Louisiana Medicaid Program, LDH or ULM; Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Must be a graduate of an ACPE accredited School/College of Pharmacy with a B.S. degree or higher; A Pharm.D. degree or equivalent work-related experience is preferred; Position requires a current Louisiana Pharmacist License or eligibility for licensure in Louisiana; Pharmacist license must be in good standing; Position requires experience with Microsoft Office (Microsoft 365) applications, good interpersonal communication skills, and exceptional organization skills with attention to detail; Self-motivation and the ability to work on a team or individually with minimal supervision are required; and Experience in or knowledge of pharmacy policy is preferred. Supplemental Information Required Attachments: Please provide a CV/Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5517056/tech-support-supervisor": {
      "title": "Tech Support Supervisor",
      "description": "Tech Support Supervisor Salary $48,000.00 - $58,000.00 Annually Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01796 Division Business Affairs Department Information Technology Opening Date 10/14/2026 Control Number 9048 Description Benefits Job Summary The Tech Support Supervisor will be in charge of support and operation of campus computer systems as well as providing supervision of the Lab Coordinator and the A/V Classroom Coordinator. This is a Tier 2 level support position. Duties and Responsibilities Manage technology deployment and coordination of new computer purchases, printer purchases, and mobile device purchases. Create, maintain and deploy software images for use on campus-wide and lab systems, both Mac and PC Coordinate with faculty/staff to acquire quotes for new PC purchases as well as new printer purchases from Dell and Apple. Maintains contact with all academic departments to ensure that their computer-based needs are met. Work with the departments on computer updates as needed. Creates new computer specifications based on current technologies. Coordinates all software installations and support with faculty/staff who have specific software requirements. Recommends procedures to enhance use of academic computing resources. Coordinates any warranty or repair requests from Dell and Apple. Required to maintain a current Dell Certified System Expert status in order to perform authorized warranty repairs on Dell equipment and ensure other select technicians do the same. Monitors and evaluates end user systems for performance using technical skills attained through training and experience. Responsible for planning and implementation of campus-wide PC management policies. Responsible for maintaining and monitoring Verizon mobile phone accounts and ordering mobile devices as needed. Supervises the Lab Coordinator and the A/V Classroom Coordinator positions. Other duties as required. Minimum Qualifications Must have bachelor’s degree or at least 5 years of real-world field experience in technical based background. Must have working TCP/IP knowledge. Experience in Microsoft products – Windows 11, Windows Server, MS Office; lab imaging software; Apple OS platform knowledge preferred. Experience with Active Directory and remote management software preferred. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5475436/visiting-instructor-of-music": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor of Music",
      "description": "Visiting Instructor of Music Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time 9-month Faculty Job Number 01778 Division Academic Affairs Department College of Arts, Education, & Sciences Opening Date 09/08/2026 Control Number 9015 Description Benefits Job Summary The successful candidate will be an exceptional collaborative artist and pianist with demonstrated excellence in teaching and a successful record of performance in a variety of genres. Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Serve as principal accompanist for the ULM Choral ensembles; serve as rehearsal accompanist and vocal coach for opera and music theatre productions; serve as collaborative pianist on faculty and student performances. Participation in recruitment efforts is also expected. Additional duties may be included based upon the interests and qualifications of the successful candidate. Duties may include teaching applied voice, music literature courses, and music education courses. Final assignment of duties will be based on the needs of the music program and qualifications of the candidate. Minimum Qualifications M.M. minimum: Completed doctorate or ABD, and experience teaching at the collegiate-level preferred. Experience providing vocal coaching to music majors and minors is desired. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
