    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5524225/chief-student-affairs-officer": {
      "title": "Chief Student Affairs Officer",
      "description": "Chief Student Affairs Officer Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01800 Division Student Affairs Opening Date 10/21/2026 Control Number 9053 Description Benefits Job Summary The Chief Student Affairs Officer reports to the President works closely with other direct reports to the President. This person serves as the primary advocate for students and for campus life and engagement activities and planning. Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the chief student affairs professional for the university. Provide guidance, oversight, and supervision of select student affairs departments including Student Advocacy and Accountability, Counseling, Residential Life/Housing, Student Development, Accessibility Services, International Student Services, Antihazing, and Student Conduct. Oversight may evolve as a result of organization. Supervise Directors and other staff within the assigned division, conducting annual evaluations and supporting professional development. Provide leadership during crisis situations, such as student mental health emergencies, campus safety events and help coordinate institutional response. Manage division budget allocations and fiscal oversight of assigned units, ensuring compliance with institutional financial requirements. Lead division-wide assessment, design program evaluations, and report outcomes to President. Support Institutional Effectiveness unit in accreditation, as it relates to student affairs Compile assessment data and reports for reporting units. Build and maintain collaborative relationships with other departments to advance student success. It is expected to have a close working relationship with auxiliary services, enrollment management, career services, and other student related functions. Develop and facilitate programs for the student community centered on student advocacy, accountability, and awareness. Ensure policies and practices of reporting units assure fair and consistent student treatment. Assist with evaluating, creating, and updating campus policies applicable to the student community. Verify that student services offered at ULM are effective, innovative, proactive, anticipatory and responsive to student and community requirements with periodic program, service, procedures and policies evaluations. Provide vision and guidance for traditional student engagement programs such as Freshman Convocation, Week of Welcome, Homecoming, Spring Fever, and Midnight Breakfast. Explore innovative practices to allow the university to remain in line with field trends and best practices. Work with team members to establish civic-centered student initiates that enhance the educational experience while furthering the brand of ULM. Network with campus professionals and student organizations to ensure there is awareness of campus resources and support services. Network with peer professionals off campus. Serve on university committees as assigned. Participate in professional development activities on and off campus to maintain a satisfactory knowledge base. Other duties as assigned by supervisor Minimum Qualifications Required: Master’s degree in education, educational leadership, student affairs, higher education, or other applicable field from an accredited institution At least five years of professional experience in related work Previous experience working in a higher education setting Experience with budget management, identifying efficiencies and budget reduction measures Experience working in a student services or student affairs office Supervision experience Familiarity with relevant legal and governance issues at the campus, local, state, and federal levels Knowledge of student development theory Ability to utilize computer software to draft professional correspondence and other published works associated with the position Experience serving a broad range of student populations in a state university or similar setting Evidence of an energetic and innovative student-centered approach to program development and delivery Availability to provide 24/7 response to student situations (may be remote responses when applicable) Ability to work evenings and weekends during fall/spring semesters with prior notice Preferred: Doctorate Degree with a concentration in in education, educational leadership, student affairs, higher education, or other applicable field from an accredited institution Over five years of professional experience in related work Experience as a department head in higher education Experience relating to student conduct procedures Knowledge of federal and state regulations including, but not limited to Clery Act, VAWA, Campus SAVE Act, Caleb Wilson Hazing Prevention Act, Title IX and Power-Based Violence Experience supervising full-time employees Supplemental Information None Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/ulm/jobs/5529297/provost-and-vice-president-for-academic-affairs": {
      "title": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 700 University Avenue, Monroe, LA, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number 01802 Division Academic Affairs Department VP for Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/26/2026 Control Number 0000 Description Benefits Job Summary The Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs serves as the chief academic officer of the University. The Provost is responsible for maintaining the academic integrity of the university and ensures that all policies and procedures related to Academic Affairs for federal, state, University of Louisiana System, and the Board of Regents are carefully followed. Duties and Responsibilities Serve as the Chief Academic Officer, overseeing academic programs and various student support services. Oversees the proper functioning of the University Colleges and Graduate Student Services, Honors Program and the operations of the Office of Academic Affairs. Establishes all academic policies, oversees reviews of all academic units, leads and implements strategic planning for academic affairs, including a comprehensive academic master plan. Coordinates with the President and other Vice Presidents to develop the University’s annual operating and capital outlay budgets for submission to the University of Louisiana System, Board of Regents, and the Louisiana Legislature. Ensures the quality and integrity of all academic programs, including program and accreditation reviews, annual reports for new degree programs to supervisory boards, and curriculum development. Evaluates the performance of all tenure and promotion candidates, ensuring tenure and promotion decisions are based on approved guidelines. Manages budgets and allocates funds appropriately to meet the needs of academic, co-curricular, and support units within Academic Affairs. Enforces the policies and rules of the University, the University of Louisiana System Board of Supervisors, and the Louisiana Board of Regents. Adjudicates policies and procedures of the Faculty and Student Handbook. Oversees and coordinates all reaffirmation efforts as mandated by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges. Provides guidance for all programmatic accreditations, connecting all accreditation efforts to the University’s mission and strategic plan. Encourages and supports excellence in teaching, research/professional activity, and service. Maintains strong, healthy community, public, and legislative relations for the benefit of the University. Assists with University development activities, including public and private fund raising. Works closely with the University of Louisiana System and the Louisiana Board of Regents on System and University activities. Creates and maintains a positive climate within all academic and student support units and supports effective communication and interaction among units. Supports close working relationships with community and technical colleges, particularly Delta Community College, as well as other Louisiana school systems. Represents the University in speaking engagements and public appearances both on and off campus. Represents the University on the Council of Vice Presidents of Academic Affairs advising University of Louisiana System Board of Supervisors and the System staff. Represents the University in a leadership capacity for community organizations and activities; Performs the responsibilities of the President if he/she is unable; and may perform any other job-related duties as assigned by the President. Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree from an accredited University and a record of scholarship commensurate with a tenured full professor in a discipline at ULM; Substantial higher education senior administrative experience (5+ years) as a dean (or equivalent) or higher; have vision, integrity, creativity, energy, and acumen; preferred experience as Provost or Vice President. Collegial, collaborative, and diplomatic; Strong communication skills. Employees are eligible for a full benefits package (health, dental, vision, life, retirement, leave, etc.) ULM offers a wide range of employee benefits. Read here for more information regarding benefits. Employer University of Louisiana Monroe Address 700 University Avenue Monroe, Louisiana, 71209 Phone 318-342-5140 Website http://www.ulm.edu Apply"
    }
  },
